{"module":"2e semestre","title":"Le calcul trigonométrique (1)","description":"Radian, cercle trigonométrique, cosinus, sinus, tangente, relations et valeurs remarquables.","intro":"On repère les angles sur le cercle trigonométrique en radians et on définit cosinus, sinus et tangente d’un réel.","objectifs":["Convertir degrés ⟷ radians.","Connaître les valeurs remarquables.","Utiliser les relations trigonométriques."],"cours":[{"t":"Radian et cercle trigonométrique","h":"<div class=\"formula key\">π rad = 180°</div><p>Le cercle trigonométrique a pour rayon 1 et est orienté dans le sens direct (inverse des aiguilles d’une montre). Un réel x a une infinité d’abscisses curvilignes x + 2kπ ; l’<b>abscisse curviligne principale</b> est celle de ]−π ; π].</p>"},{"t":"Cosinus, sinus, tangente","h":"<p>Si M est le point associé à x, cos x est l’abscisse de M et sin x son ordonnée.</p><div class=\"formula key\">cos²x + sin²x = 1</div><ul><li>−1 ≤ cos x ≤ 1 et −1 ≤ sin x ≤ 1</li><li>tan x = sin x / cos x (cos x ≠ 0) et 1 + tan²x = 1/cos²x</li></ul><table><tr><th>x</th><th>0</th><th>π/6</th><th>π/4</th><th>π/3</th><th>π/2</th></tr><tr><td>cos x</td><td>1</td><td>√3/2</td><td>√2/2</td><td>1/2</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>sin x</td><td>0</td><td>1/2</td><td>√2/2</td><td>√3/2</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>tan x</td><td>0</td><td>√3/3</td><td>1</td><td>√3</td><td>—</td></tr></table>"},{"t":"Relations utiles","h":"<ul><li>cos(−x) = cos x ; sin(−x) = −sin x</li><li>cos(π − x) = −cos x ; sin(π − x) = sin x</li><li>cos(π + x) = −cos x ; sin(π + x) = −sin x</li><li>cos(π/2 − x) = sin x ; sin(π/2 − x) = cos x</li></ul>"}],"recap":"π rad = 180°. cos²x + sin²x = 1. cos(π − x) = −cos x, sin(π − x) = sin x. Valeurs : cos(π/3) = 1/2, sin(π/6) = 1/2, cos(π/4) = √2/2.","cards":[["π rad","180°"],["cos² + sin²","= 1"],["sin(π − x)","= sin x"],["1 + tan²x","= 1 / cos²x"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"calc","q":"60° = π/n radians. Donne n.","answer":3,"explain":"60° = 180°/3 = π/3.","tol":0,"sci":false},{"type":"calc","q":"Donne cos(π/3) (en décimal).","answer":0.5,"explain":"cos(π/3) = 1/2.","tol":0.001,"sci":false},{"type":"qcm","q":"cos²x + sin²x =","choices":["1","0","2","cos 2x"],"answer":0,"explain":"Relation fondamentale (Pythagore dans le cercle de rayon 1)."}],"moyen":[{"type":"calc","q":"Convertis 3π/4 rad en degrés.","answer":135,"explain":"3 × 180/4 = 135°.","tol":0,"sci":false},{"type":"qcm","q":"sin(π − x) =","choices":["sin x","−sin x","cos x","−cos x"],"answer":0,"explain":"π − x est le symétrique de x par rapport à l’axe des ordonnées : même sinus."},{"type":"calc","q":"cos x = 0,6 et sin x > 0. Calcule sin x.","answer":0.8,"explain":"sin²x = 1 − 0,36 = 0,64 ⟹ sin x = 0,8 (positif).","tol":0.001,"sci":false}],"difficile":[{"type":"calc","q":"A(x) = cos(π − x) + cos(π + x) + 2cos x. Pour tout x, A(x) = ?","answer":0,"explain":"−cos x − cos x + 2cos x = 0.","tol":0,"sci":false},{"type":"calc","q":"tan x = 2. Calcule 1/cos²x.","answer":5,"explain":"1 + tan²x = 1 + 4 = 5.","tol":0,"sci":false},{"type":"qcm","q":"L’abscisse curviligne principale de 7π/3 est :","choices":["π/3","7π/3","−π/3","2π/3"],"answer":0,"explain":"7π/3 = π/3 + 2π, et π/3 ∈ ]−π ; π].","why":[null,"7π/3 > π : ce n’est pas l’abscisse principale.","Le signe est faux.","7π/3 − 2π = π/3, pas 2π/3."]}]},"ar":{"title":"الحساب المثلثي (1)","cours":[{"t":"الراديان والدائرة المثلثية","h":"<p><b>π rad = 180°</b>.</p><p>الدائرة المثلثية شعاعها 1 وموجهة في المنحى المباشر (عكس عقارب الساعة). لكل عدد x ما لا نهاية من الأفاصيل المنحنية x + 2kπ، والأفصول الرئيسي هو الذي ينتمي إلى ]−π ; π].</p>"},{"t":"جيب التمام والجيب والظل","h":"<p>إذا كانت M النقطة المرتبطة بـ x، فإن cos x هو أفصول M و sin x هو أرتوبها.</p><p><b>cos²x + sin²x = 1</b>، وكل من cos x و sin x محصور بين −1 و 1.</p><p>tan x = sin x / cos x. القيم الهامة: cos(π/3) = 1/2، sin(π/6) = 1/2، cos(π/4) = sin(π/4) = √2/2.</p>"},{"t":"علاقات مفيدة","h":"<p>cos(−x) = cos x و sin(−x) = −sin x.</p><p>cos(π − x) = −cos x و sin(π − x) = sin x، و cos(π + x) = −cos x و sin(π + x) = −sin x.</p><p>cos(π/2 − x) = sin x و sin(π/2 − x) = cos x. يمكن رؤية كل هذه العلاقات بالتماثلات على الدائرة.</p>"}]}}